dx: bil pna, sepsis; ruled in for MI      Pt DNR/DNI

89 yo h/o CAD, DM, CHF, presented w/ nausea, vomiting at home per ED report, though pt denies n/v; states she was in the bathroom, slipped, hit her head; head and neck CTs neg; denies cp, sz, loss of bowel/bladder control;
   found febrile in ED, CXR showed bil pna; was 80% on RA, O2 sat increased to 95% w/ face mask at 100%; also had new afib w/ ?ST depression in V3-6; received 2-3 L IVF in ED, started on Levoflox;
   pt and family refused CVL;

This night, 21:30 labs showed troponin 0.45, suggesting acute MI d/t also w/ EKG changes stated above;
   new orders for hep bolus followed by heparin gtt; already on ASA; started on statin, lopressor started, though at decreased dose d/t current sepsis;

Pt very difficult IV access; received new #20 Rt a.c. during the evening, able to draw labs off; using at this time for IVF's, IV Abx; will also use for blood transfusion; unable to obtain any more IV access this night;
   requisition for PRBC sent at 01:00, received call from blood bank that they had no speciment for cross matching; also that pt has hx of antibodies, and would take awhile to cross match;
   when unit of PRBC available, will run in over 2 hrs, necessitating stop of heparin gtt x 2 hours, MD made aware;

Pt on 5 l nc, is mouth breather when asleep, if nose breather would probably only need 2-3 l nc; assisted w/ use of incentive spirometer;

PLAN:
1) follow pt exam
2) assist pt w/ Incentive Spirometer
3) hep gtt
4) 1 unit PRBC's, when avail from blood bank
5) a.m. labs will be drawn approx 4 or 5 a.m., blood will be transfused following over two hours, hep gtt will be interrupted during thoses 2 hours;
6) address access issue in a.m.
7) abx as ordered
